body:
Title: Add structured output example w/ Zod validation + strict/lenient parsing guidance; add snippet tests

Context / Why: We have recurring drift between docs snippets and SDK examples for “structured output” (aka schema-based JSON responses). Support has multiple tickets where customers copy an older snippet and either (a) accept invalid JSON silently, or (b) fail hard with unclear errors when the model returns JSON that’s close-but-not-valid for their schema. This PR adds a canonical TypeScript example that: (1) requests structured output via JSON schema, (2) validates with Zod, and (3) documents two patterns: strict (fail fast) vs lenient (best-effort parse + explicit retry strategy). It also adds snippet tests so we don’t regress on event/response shapes during the broader examples refresh.

What changed (high level): Added examples/structured-output/validated_zod.ts showing response_format: json_schema with a minimal schema + Zod validator, plus a small helper for retrying on parse/validation failures; Added a short “Strict vs Lenient parsing” section to the README/docs snippets for structured output (explicitly calling out when to use each, and how to surface validation errors); Added snippet test harness wiring for the structured output example (runs against mock server in CI; optional staging run behind a flag).

Example (illustrative):

const TicketSchema = z.object({ id: z.string(), priority: z.enum(["low","medium","high"]), summary: z.string().min(1) });

const schema = {
  name: "support_ticket",
  strict: true,
  schema: {
    type: "object",
    additionalProperties: false,
    properties: {
      id: { type: "string" },
      priority: { type: "string", enum: ["low","medium","high"] },
      summary: { type: "string" }
    },
    required: ["id","priority","summary"]
  }
};

const resp = await client.responses.create({
  model: "redwood/verified-open-model",
  input: "Create a support ticket for: streaming disconnects behind proxy",
  response_format: { type: "json_schema", json_schema: schema }
});

// NOTE: structured output should be parsed from the final response, not incremental stream deltas.
const raw = resp.output_text; // string
const parsedJson = JSON.parse(raw);
const ticket = TicketSchema.parse(parsedJson);

Strict vs lenient parsing guidance included in the example: Strict = JSON.parse + zod.parse; on error, surface error + retry with a corrective prompt (bounded retries). Lenient = attempt JSON repair only if you can do it safely, then zod.safeParse; if still invalid, retry or fallback to non-structured response (but do not silently accept).

Implementation details: The example uses Zod for runtime validation and includes a recommended error shape to log (redacting raw prompt/PII). Retry helper uses maxAttempts=2 by default with jittered backoff; abortable via AbortSignal so apps can enforce end-to-end timeouts; Snippet tests run under pnpm test:snippets and validate: (a) request payload includes response_format json_schema, (b) parsing/validation passes against a mocked “good” response, and (c) parse failure path produces actionable error text.

Files / Areas changed: examples/structured-output/validated_zod.ts; examples/structured-output/README.md; src/__tests__/snippets/structured_output.test.ts; scripts/snippet-runner/*; package.json (add test:snippets); docs/ snippets for structured output (TS only) and cross-links to redwood-examples.

Testing: pnpm test; pnpm lint; pnpm test:snippets (mock server). Optional: SNIPPETS_STAGING=1 pnpm test:snippets (not enabled by default in PR CI).

Rollout / Notes: No API surface changes; examples + tests only. The example explicitly cautions against trusting partially streamed JSON deltas for validation; validate only on final aggregated output. This aligns with the canonical event model being documented under ENG-2842.

Review conversation:

- Ibrahim Khan: “Can we avoid ‘JSON mode’ terminology and stick to ‘structured output’ everywhere? Also call out that Zod is validation only; JSON schema is what we send to the API.” Dana Lo: Updated headings + inline comments to use “structured output” consistently; added a small note: ‘We send JSON schema to Redwood; we use Zod to validate client-side.’

- Henry Cho: “Retry guidance: please bound attempts and include suggestion for corrective prompt (e.g., ‘Return JSON that matches the schema exactly; no extra keys’). Also, please avoid recommending JSON ‘repair’ unless we clearly label it as optional/unsafe.” Dana Lo: Added maxAttempts default + example corrective instruction; removed “repair” from the main path and moved it to an explicitly optional section with warnings.

- Sahana Iyer: “Snippet tests should not hit staging by default; ensure no secrets required.” Dana Lo: Kept staging behind SNIPPETS_STAGING=1; mock server is default; added docstring in scripts/snippet-runner/README.

- Wei Chen: “Docs snippet should mention how to surface schema mismatch errors to users.” Dana Lo: Added a short callout on logging parse vs validation errors, plus how to return a 502/500 vs 400 depending on where the failure occurred.

CI:
- Initial run failed: eslint: no-unused-vars in example (fixed by removing unused helper)
- Current status: ✅ build, ✅ unit, ✅ lint, ✅ snippet tests

Commits (squash merge): 1) examples: add validated structured output example (zod + json_schema) 2) docs: add strict vs lenient parsing guidance 3) tests: add snippet runner coverage for structured output

Merge: Squash merged into main.
